{"id": "P01410", "name": "Alejandro Bulgheroni", "name_chinese": "亚历杭德罗·布尔杰罗尼", "country": "Argentina", "net_worth_usd_m": "4945.8", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Oil & gas", "industry": "energy", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2011-2025); Hurun Global (2014-2026)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/alejandro-bulgheroni/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Alejandro Bulgheroni and his late brother Carlos (d. Sept. 2016) took over Argentine energy company Bridas Corp., founded by their father, in 1985.", "The Bulgheroni brothers sold a 50% stake in Bridas to China's state-owned offshore oil company, CNOOC, for $3.1 billion in 2011.", "In September 2017 BC Energy entered into a cash-free agreement with BP to form Pan American Energy Group, the largest privately-owned integrated energy company in Argentina.", "Bulgheroni owns more than 10 vineyards across the world, including Bodegas Garzon in Uruguay, one of the country's main exporting wineries.", "His agro-industrial complex Estancias del Lago has over 13,000 dairy cows producing an average of 550,000 liters of milk a day."], "forbes_facts": ["The membership fee for Bulgheroni's private wine club, The Garzon Club, will set you back $200,000."]}
